WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.333 --> 00:00:02.202
Joe: From calorie count to portion sizes, 

00:00:02.202 --> 00:00:06.940
we wanted to find out all the differences between McDonald's in India and the US.

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:08.842
Joe: This is "Food Wars."

00:00:12.612 --> 00:00:15.281
Drinks in McDonald's
India come in three sizes:

00:00:15.281 --> 00:00:17.817
regular, medium, and large.

00:00:17.817 --> 00:00:20.754
Drinks in the McDonald's
in the US, four sizes:

00:00:20.754 --> 00:00:24.190
extra small, small, medium, and large.

00:00:27.093 --> 00:00:28.661
Time to keep 'em honest.

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:33.800
Lost a couple drops. 26, 27 fluid ounces.

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.502
Whoo!

00:00:35.502 --> 00:00:38.004
Hm.

00:00:38.004 --> 00:00:39.973
Fries in India come in three sizes:

00:00:39.973 --> 00:00:42.208
regular, medium, and large.

00:00:42.208 --> 00:00:46.346
In America, our fries come
in four sizes, I think.

00:00:46.346 --> 00:00:49.315
We have a small, kids,

00:00:49.315 --> 00:00:52.085
or kids, small —

00:00:52.085 --> 00:00:54.187
I can't tell the difference either —

00:00:54.187 --> 00:00:56.423
medium, and large.

00:00:56.423 --> 00:00:58.658
The medium and large
come in these really cool

00:00:58.658 --> 00:01:01.561
new packaging where you can
just open it up like that

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:02.929
and it's nice and easy to share.

00:01:02.929 --> 00:01:04.064
It's a little plate.

00:01:04.064 --> 00:01:05.899
Good job, McDonald's. Very innovative.

00:01:05.899 --> 00:01:07.500
But now it's time to measure

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.369
and see how much we're really getting.

00:01:09.369 --> 00:01:11.271
Joe: First things first, the large.

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:15.175
175 grams.

00:01:15.175 --> 00:01:17.377
Obviously it's different
per scoops or whatever.

00:01:17.377 --> 00:01:18.411
Yeah, let's go here.

00:01:18.411 --> 00:01:22.048
This one, almost exactly 100 grams.

00:01:22.048 --> 00:01:23.983
This one,

00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:25.085
80 grams.

00:01:25.085 --> 00:01:26.286
Fry math, hang on.

00:01:28.388 --> 00:01:29.989
This is, like...

00:01:29.989 --> 00:01:30.990
yep, there you go.

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:32.425
That's a 20-gram difference right there.

00:01:32.425 --> 00:01:33.927
So, you tell me, internet.

00:01:33.927 --> 00:01:35.829
Is the kids and the small different sizes?

00:01:35.829 --> 00:01:36.896
I don't think they are.

00:01:36.896 --> 00:01:39.966
"Food Wars" is on it! We're on it, baby!

00:01:39.966 --> 00:01:40.934
What about McNuggets?

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:44.070
Here in India, you can
order them in three sizes:

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:47.807
six pieces, nine pieces, and 20 pieces.

00:01:47.807 --> 00:01:50.677
They gave it to us in
two boxes of 10 each.

00:01:50.677 --> 00:01:52.645
Oh, is that it, India? Cute.

00:01:52.645 --> 00:01:55.248
Our McNuggets start at four,

00:01:55.248 --> 00:01:56.683
then you got six,

00:01:56.683 --> 00:01:58.017
10,

00:01:58.017 --> 00:01:59.252
20,

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:00.620
and not to be outdone,

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:03.056
booyah, 40 McNuggets.

00:02:03.056 --> 00:02:05.592
All the mathheads watching
will be quick to point out

00:02:05.592 --> 00:02:09.596
that that is double India's
largest nugget option.

00:02:09.596 --> 00:02:11.898
The only burger that
India shares with the US

00:02:11.898 --> 00:02:14.534
is the McChicken, 
the humble McChicken.

00:02:14.534 --> 00:02:17.570
Not even gonna bother
with the analog scale now.

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:18.738
Boop!

00:02:18.738 --> 00:02:20.840
149 grams.

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:23.109
Ah, just so frustrating.

00:02:23.109 --> 00:02:25.678
Just one more gram and
it would be perfect.

00:02:25.678 --> 00:02:28.414
With the paper? I mean, we'll do this and

00:02:29.649 --> 00:02:32.752
shave off an eighth of an ounce.

00:02:32.752 --> 00:02:36.923
Our McChicken weighs 140 grams.

00:02:39.292 --> 00:02:40.660
Here is everything you'll find on the menu

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:43.830
at McDonald's India that you
will not find in the USA.

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:45.431
And here's all the McDonald's menu items

00:02:45.431 --> 00:02:48.601
from the US you won't find in India.

00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:50.303
Here in India, we can't really recreate

00:02:50.303 --> 00:02:52.071
the iconic McDonald's Big Mac

00:02:52.071 --> 00:02:53.973
because it's made from a beef patty,

00:02:53.973 --> 00:02:56.075
and to keep to the religious sentiments

00:02:56.075 --> 00:02:57.744
of Hindus and even Muslims,

00:02:57.744 --> 00:02:59.012
we don't serve beef or pork

00:02:59.012 --> 00:03:00.580
in a lot of fast-food restaurants.

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:04.484
We have something called
the chicken Maharaja Mac.

00:03:04.484 --> 00:03:08.588
As you can see, it's got
three buns, two patties,

00:03:08.588 --> 00:03:11.157
a lot of cheese and mayonnaise,

00:03:11.157 --> 00:03:13.893
some tomatoes, onions, lettuce.

00:03:13.893 --> 00:03:16.829
Lettuce try it now.
[ba-dum tish]

00:03:18.364 --> 00:03:20.033
Oh, my God.

00:03:20.033 --> 00:03:22.402
That is truly a Maharaja Mac.

00:03:22.402 --> 00:03:24.737
If you're wondering, a raja is a king,

00:03:24.737 --> 00:03:27.006
and a maharaja is like an emperor.

00:03:27.006 --> 00:03:29.576
So this is clearly our
answer to the Big Mac.

00:03:29.576 --> 00:03:31.611
Now let's taste the veg Maharaja Mac.

00:03:31.611 --> 00:03:33.379
I think it's actually
a very cool challenge

00:03:33.379 --> 00:03:34.781
that a lot of fast-food restaurants here

00:03:34.781 --> 00:03:36.482
have had to adapt to the Indian palate,

00:03:36.482 --> 00:03:39.285
as well as sensibilities of food.

00:03:39.285 --> 00:03:41.955
We have come up with such
cool, iconic fast food

00:03:41.955 --> 00:03:43.957
that you won't get
anywhere else in the world.

00:03:43.957 --> 00:03:46.192
Like, look at this! This is outrageous!

00:03:46.192 --> 00:03:48.661
There's no way to eat
this without being messy.

00:03:48.661 --> 00:03:49.996
There's literally no way.

00:03:52.999 --> 00:03:54.000
Mm!

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:56.135
Oh, my God. That's really good.

00:03:56.135 --> 00:03:58.471
Yes to all that, looks really good.

00:03:58.471 --> 00:04:01.007
Because of India's lack of beef,

00:04:01.007 --> 00:04:03.977
all the American beef options
are technically exclusives.

00:04:08.081 --> 00:04:09.315
All right.

00:04:09.315 --> 00:04:10.383
Big Mac.

00:04:10.383 --> 00:04:14.354
There it is, just brimming with stuff.

00:04:14.354 --> 00:04:16.256
My go-to for, like, 20 years.

00:04:16.256 --> 00:04:17.824
I still get it occasionally.

00:04:17.824 --> 00:04:20.760
The classic McDonald's hamburger.

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:22.862
Beef patty, ketchup, and mustard.

00:04:22.862 --> 00:04:26.666
Of course, you can get it with cheese. Hi.

00:04:26.666 --> 00:04:30.069
You can upgrade to a double
cheeseburger or a McDouble.

00:04:30.069 --> 00:04:31.838
What's the difference, you ask?

00:04:31.838 --> 00:04:33.039
I'm not sure either.

00:04:33.039 --> 00:04:35.742
So let's start with the
double cheeseburger.

00:04:35.742 --> 00:04:37.477
Look at that. Look how yellow that is.

00:04:37.477 --> 00:04:40.346
Beef, cheese, beef, cheese, toppos.

00:04:40.346 --> 00:04:45.151
The McDouble is beef, cheese, beef.

00:04:45.151 --> 00:04:46.786
So it's just one slice of cheese

00:04:46.786 --> 00:04:48.087
in the middle, but not on top.

00:04:48.087 --> 00:04:50.923
What's the price difference?
Can we get that on-screen?

00:04:50.923 --> 00:04:52.725
And how much is a slice of cheese?

00:04:53.593 --> 00:04:55.161
Joe's hack, get yourself a McDouble

00:04:55.161 --> 00:04:57.030
and bring your own slice
of American cheese.

00:04:57.030 --> 00:04:59.899
Booyah. Save yourself
this amount of money.

00:04:59.899 --> 00:05:02.001
The problem with millennials today,

00:05:02.001 --> 00:05:04.070
the reason you guys can't buy houses is

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:06.406
you're spending all
your money at Starbucks,

00:05:06.406 --> 00:05:08.875
you're getting your double cheeseburgers

00:05:08.875 --> 00:05:12.211
instead of a McDouble and
bringing your own cheese slice.

00:05:12.211 --> 00:05:14.280
I mean, you guys are terrible with money!

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:15.715
You're eating, what, seven,

00:05:15.715 --> 00:05:17.317
eight McDoubles a day like me, right?

00:05:17.317 --> 00:05:21.020
And that adds up to, like,
at the end of the year, $18?

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:24.223
10,000 years later, that's
a down payment on a house.

00:05:25.558 --> 00:05:26.759
What are you guys doing?

00:05:26.759 --> 00:05:30.897
All right, next up is the
iconic McAloo tikki burger.

00:05:30.897 --> 00:05:33.766
You take mashed potato, and
you fry it in breadcrumbs,

00:05:33.766 --> 00:05:35.835
and you get this really delicious cutlet.

00:05:35.835 --> 00:05:39.005
Here in India, they
adapted it into this burger

00:05:39.005 --> 00:05:40.873
with a very special sauce,

00:05:40.873 --> 00:05:43.209
some tomato, and chopped onions.

00:05:45.545 --> 00:05:47.814
Mm. It's just so classic.

00:05:47.814 --> 00:05:49.349
They nailed this burger.

00:05:49.349 --> 00:05:52.051
Next up, there is a Mexican McAloo tikki,

00:05:52.051 --> 00:05:55.855
which I assume has some
stereotypical Mexican ingredients

00:05:55.855 --> 00:05:58.558
and flavors like jalapeño.

00:05:58.558 --> 00:06:00.593
Yes! Jalapeño.

00:06:00.593 --> 00:06:01.794
Mm, nice.

00:06:01.794 --> 00:06:04.364
It's way more spicy. Good twist.

00:06:04.364 --> 00:06:07.333
Next up, they have a McEgg burger.

00:06:07.333 --> 00:06:09.569
McEgg. McEgg, McEgg.

00:06:09.569 --> 00:06:10.970
I don't know why I did that.

00:06:10.970 --> 00:06:12.505
Let's see what that looks like.

00:06:12.505 --> 00:06:13.906
Ugh!

00:06:13.906 --> 00:06:15.007
Sorry.

00:06:15.007 --> 00:06:17.110
I did not expect... pesto?

00:06:17.110 --> 00:06:19.479
Next up is a chicken kebab burger.

00:06:19.479 --> 00:06:22.081
Every time an Indian
fast-food chain tries to adapt

00:06:22.081 --> 00:06:25.651
an Indian special food into a burger,

00:06:25.651 --> 00:06:27.120
I take it with a pinch of salt

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:29.188
because this is not what
we're used to seeing

00:06:29.188 --> 00:06:30.189
when we think of kebabs,

00:06:30.189 --> 00:06:33.326
but I'm going to try it,
and let's see what happens.

00:06:33.326 --> 00:06:34.627
Mm.

00:06:34.627 --> 00:06:36.262
It's very, very dry.

00:06:36.262 --> 00:06:39.232
Patty has almost a
cardboard-y taste to it.

00:06:39.232 --> 00:06:41.234
I wouldn't put those flavors together

00:06:41.234 --> 00:06:43.469
if I was thinking kebab.

00:06:43.469 --> 00:06:46.372
McCardboard tikki, maybe? No? OK.

00:06:46.372 --> 00:06:47.707
That's a bit harsh. I'm sorry.

00:06:47.707 --> 00:06:49.609
Next up is the McVeggie,

00:06:49.609 --> 00:06:53.579
which is the vegetarian
counterpart to our McChicken.

00:06:53.579 --> 00:06:56.449
If I had to eat this
versus the chicken one,

00:06:56.449 --> 00:06:58.518
I would not be upset at all.

00:06:58.518 --> 00:06:59.452
Really good.

00:06:59.452 --> 00:07:01.654
Next up, we have two "American" burgers:

00:07:01.654 --> 00:07:04.724
the American Cheese Supreme veg

00:07:04.724 --> 00:07:08.194
and the American Cheese Supreme chicken.

00:07:08.194 --> 00:07:09.996
My hunch for what makes them American

00:07:09.996 --> 00:07:13.499
is that they will have a
nice big square of cheese

00:07:13.499 --> 00:07:16.569
and they will not be spicy at all.

00:07:16.569 --> 00:07:19.739
Except they have a lot
of jalapeños on them.

00:07:19.739 --> 00:07:24.277
Joe, let me know if this
constitutes "American."

00:07:24.277 --> 00:07:25.878
That's American cheese, my man.

00:07:25.878 --> 00:07:27.280
That's what makes it American.

00:07:27.280 --> 00:07:28.815
I don't know about those
other toppings, but,

00:07:28.815 --> 00:07:29.682
yeah, it sounds about right.

00:07:29.682 --> 00:07:31.384
All right, so this is what
the McDonald's website

00:07:31.384 --> 00:07:33.419
says is in this burger.

00:07:33.419 --> 00:07:36.189
"Whole-wheat buns
sourced from Maharashtra,

00:07:36.189 --> 00:07:38.724
tangy jalapeños from Karnataka,

00:07:38.724 --> 00:07:42.128
shredded onions grown
in local Indian farms,

00:07:42.128 --> 00:07:46.499
and cheese from Amaravati, also in India."

00:07:46.499 --> 00:07:49.368
Quite close to home, this burger.

00:07:49.368 --> 00:07:51.971
Currently, this would
probably be my favorite order,

00:07:51.971 --> 00:07:54.907
a McSpicy chicken, and
there's the vegetarian option,

00:07:54.907 --> 00:07:58.678
which is a McSpicy paneer,
which is just leaking lettuce.

00:07:58.678 --> 00:08:00.279
For those of you who
don't know what paneer is,

00:08:00.279 --> 00:08:02.281
it's basically cottage cheese.

00:08:02.281 --> 00:08:03.516
We love our paneer.

00:08:03.516 --> 00:08:06.519
We put it in curries, we eat
it plain, we put it in kebabs.

00:08:06.519 --> 00:08:09.055
It is so delicious. Let's try this.

00:08:11.257 --> 00:08:13.726
Mm. It has just the right kick,

00:08:13.726 --> 00:08:15.361
and it goes really well with the paneer.

00:08:15.361 --> 00:08:17.563
Fair warning, while this
may have a light kick

00:08:17.563 --> 00:08:20.500
of spice for us, it might
be a hard kick for you.

00:08:20.500 --> 00:08:24.303
So, take everything with
a pinch of chili powder.

00:08:24.303 --> 00:08:26.873
Gonna move up to something
called the Quarter Pounder,

00:08:26.873 --> 00:08:28.508
and that's, like, their big burger.

00:08:28.508 --> 00:08:30.142
So you can get a Quarter
Pounder with cheese.

00:08:30.142 --> 00:08:30.977
Here it is.

00:08:30.977 --> 00:08:32.979
I mean, it looks fake, right?

00:08:32.979 --> 00:08:34.780
Like, "Just kidding, it's cake!"

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:38.150
Or the new one is, "It's
actually a candle!"

00:08:38.150 --> 00:08:41.487
And then you can get a Quarter
Pounder with cheese deluxe.

00:08:41.487 --> 00:08:44.123
More veggies on it, all
the junk that I brush off.

00:08:44.123 --> 00:08:48.094
You can upgrade to a double
Quarter Pounder with cheese.

00:08:48.094 --> 00:08:51.664
Let's take a look. Oh, man.
Look how thick this is!

00:08:51.664 --> 00:08:55.401
And then you can get that
same double with bacon.

00:08:55.401 --> 00:08:56.569
Yeah!

00:08:56.569 --> 00:08:59.438
Oh, man. Skimping on the bacon. Guys!

00:08:59.438 --> 00:09:01.841
What we lack in beef
burgers we make up for

00:09:01.841 --> 00:09:03.943
in gourmet burgers.

00:09:03.943 --> 00:09:05.945
That's right. Here at McDonald's India,

00:09:05.945 --> 00:09:07.246
we have our own collection of

00:09:07.246 --> 00:09:10.449
chef's special gourmet burgers.

00:09:10.449 --> 00:09:11.417
Delicious.

00:09:11.417 --> 00:09:12.952
And I think this is a rolling menu.

00:09:12.952 --> 00:09:14.820
I think they introduce new
things from time to time.

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:18.524
The buns themselves
look a lot more gourmet.

00:09:18.524 --> 00:09:20.560
You know, there's a nice
rift down the middle.

00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:22.528
Kind of looks like a butt, but that's OK.

00:09:22.528 --> 00:09:24.063
We're not gonna concentrate on that.

00:09:25.097 --> 00:09:27.733
First up, we have triple
cheese American veg burger

00:09:27.733 --> 00:09:30.770
and triple cheese American 
chicken burger.

00:09:30.770 --> 00:09:34.607
Same thing. Cheese, jalapeño,
some sauce, lettuce,

00:09:34.607 --> 00:09:37.510
simple chicken patty, gourmet bun.

00:09:37.510 --> 00:09:39.045
Does this scream "American" to you?

00:09:39.045 --> 00:09:41.881
Next up, Cheese Lava American veg burger

00:09:41.881 --> 00:09:44.784
and Cheese Lava American chicken burger,

00:09:44.784 --> 00:09:46.052
again with American

00:09:46.052 --> 00:09:49.055
and again with the strange relation

00:09:49.055 --> 00:09:52.491
of food to volcanoes and lava.

00:09:53.993 --> 00:09:55.161
OK.

00:09:55.161 --> 00:09:57.263
This burger is very spicy.

00:09:57.263 --> 00:10:00.499
This qualifies as a
volcano product, for sure.

00:10:00.499 --> 00:10:02.368
Congratulations, McDonald's.

00:10:02.368 --> 00:10:05.938
The lava in the title
of this burger works.

00:10:05.938 --> 00:10:08.207
The McSpicy chicken premium, though,

00:10:08.207 --> 00:10:11.277
has an egg patty inside of it.

00:10:11.277 --> 00:10:13.613
Mm-mm.

00:10:13.613 --> 00:10:16.282
Mm, that's pretty good.

00:10:16.282 --> 00:10:18.417
I just feel so existential right now.

00:10:19.352 --> 00:10:20.953
Imagine sitting here at this table

00:10:20.953 --> 00:10:24.657
and just tasting every single
burger on a McDonald's menu.

00:10:25.825 --> 00:10:27.460
Amazing.

00:10:27.460 --> 00:10:29.395
But also, s---.

00:10:29.395 --> 00:10:31.597
We also have some exclusive wrap options.

00:10:31.597 --> 00:10:34.967
We have Big Spicy paneer
and Big Spicy chicken.

00:10:34.967 --> 00:10:38.571
I think this is the same
McSpicy chicken patty,

00:10:38.571 --> 00:10:41.140
and it's wrapped around a tortilla,

00:10:41.140 --> 00:10:43.409
which is actually way
closer to an Indian chapati

00:10:43.409 --> 00:10:44.977
than most other fast-food restaurants.

00:10:44.977 --> 00:10:47.346
It doesn't feel as synthetic.

00:10:47.346 --> 00:10:49.482
Our McDonald's in the US

00:10:49.482 --> 00:10:52.118
had wraps for a brief period of time.

00:10:52.118 --> 00:10:55.087
One day they were gone. Nobody noticed.

00:10:55.087 --> 00:10:57.123
Yeah, you guys got some chicken
stuff that we don't have,

00:10:57.123 --> 00:10:58.457
but we got a few of our own.

00:10:58.457 --> 00:11:00.192
More recently than you think,

00:11:00.192 --> 00:11:02.862
they finally introduced
their chicken sandwich

00:11:02.862 --> 00:11:06.732
to an already-crowded
chicken-sandwich market,

00:11:06.732 --> 00:11:09.068
and that is of course their
crispy chicken sandwich,

00:11:09.068 --> 00:11:12.004
and this thing is fantastic.

00:11:12.004 --> 00:11:13.406
It's one of the best ones.

00:11:13.406 --> 00:11:14.640
They were late to the game,

00:11:14.640 --> 00:11:16.275
and they kind of took
it over, in my opinion.

00:11:16.275 --> 00:11:18.711
And what I like about it,
it's simple. Look at this.

00:11:18.711 --> 00:11:21.881
You just got crispy
chicken, pickles that suck.

00:11:21.881 --> 00:11:23.315
It's baller. It tastes great.

00:11:23.315 --> 00:11:25.151
Like it a little spicy, India?

00:11:25.151 --> 00:11:26.285
It probably doesn't
compare to what you guys

00:11:26.285 --> 00:11:28.020
are rocking in India but, you know,

00:11:28.020 --> 00:11:30.256
this one has a little nice heat to it.

00:11:30.256 --> 00:11:31.557
Pickles, sauce.

00:11:31.557 --> 00:11:33.225
Want to take it up a notch?

00:11:33.225 --> 00:11:34.593
Gotta go deluxe.

00:11:34.593 --> 00:11:37.096
The cool crispness of the vegetables

00:11:37.096 --> 00:11:40.399
just clash so well with the spicy sauce.

00:11:40.399 --> 00:11:42.068
It's good. It's good.

00:11:42.068 --> 00:11:43.669
Nikhil, say the word,

00:11:43.669 --> 00:11:45.771
and I'm putting one in
the post for you tomorrow.

00:11:45.771 --> 00:11:47.206
So when it arrives in three weeks,

00:11:47.206 --> 00:11:49.008
you can throw it out.

00:11:49.008 --> 00:11:51.510
Now we're getting into
exclusive side dishes.

00:11:51.510 --> 00:11:54.280
Here in India, we have these add-ons.

00:11:54.280 --> 00:11:57.683
No. 1, the veg pizza McPuff.

00:11:57.683 --> 00:12:00.519
This is one of the most
delicious things we have here.

00:12:00.519 --> 00:12:02.688
It's basically a pizza Hot Pocket.

00:12:02.688 --> 00:12:05.024
Masala wedges. These are potato wedges

00:12:05.024 --> 00:12:08.828
with classic Indian masala flavor to them.

00:12:08.828 --> 00:12:09.995
Ooh, boy.

00:12:09.995 --> 00:12:11.864
Masalas are basically what we use

00:12:11.864 --> 00:12:13.933
to spice and flavor dishes,

00:12:13.933 --> 00:12:16.302
and they consist primarily
of ground-up spices

00:12:16.302 --> 00:12:18.437
like cardamom, cloves,

00:12:18.437 --> 00:12:20.306
red chilies, Kashmiri chilies.

00:12:20.306 --> 00:12:22.708
You go to every Indian home, the mums,

00:12:22.708 --> 00:12:25.377
the grandmums will have
their own random, you know,

00:12:25.377 --> 00:12:29.181
masala mix that they
use and that's guarded

00:12:29.181 --> 00:12:31.984
and treasured in their family, forever.

00:12:31.984 --> 00:12:34.253
Next up, we have cheesy masala wedges.

00:12:34.253 --> 00:12:38.390
They're also serving a
classic cup of boiled corn,

00:12:38.390 --> 00:12:42.828
which is so unique, and they
give you a side of Amul butter.

00:12:42.828 --> 00:12:45.765
Guys, Amul butter is part of our culture.

00:12:45.765 --> 00:12:48.701
Makhan. Makhan!

00:12:48.701 --> 00:12:49.602
This is probably going to be

00:12:49.602 --> 00:12:51.370
the most delicious bite of the day.

00:12:54.840 --> 00:12:56.041
I love corn.

00:12:56.041 --> 00:12:57.409
Next up, chicken strips.

00:12:57.409 --> 00:13:01.413
They come in packs of two, three, or five.

00:13:01.413 --> 00:13:04.383
Cheesy nugget veg bites.

00:13:04.383 --> 00:13:05.918
Yeah, this is just a vegetarian version

00:13:05.918 --> 00:13:06.819
of the chicken nuggets,

00:13:06.819 --> 00:13:09.188
and it's got some corn, some tomato.

00:13:10.389 --> 00:13:11.857
Mm, it's OK.

00:13:11.857 --> 00:13:15.694
Next, we have the double cheese McMuffin.

00:13:15.694 --> 00:13:19.598
And lastly, we have Mexican cheesy fries.

00:13:19.598 --> 00:13:21.267
On the McDonald's India website,

00:13:21.267 --> 00:13:23.402
one British customer said

00:13:23.402 --> 00:13:26.839
that these Mexican cheesy
fries are "the real deal."

00:13:26.839 --> 00:13:29.775
I have no idea how a
British person can say

00:13:29.775 --> 00:13:31.610
that Mexican cheesy
fries are the real deal,

00:13:31.610 --> 00:13:33.746
but anytime a British person says

00:13:33.746 --> 00:13:36.549
that another culture's
food is "the real deal,"

00:13:36.549 --> 00:13:40.519
it puts a little fear in
our small Indian hearts.

00:13:40.519 --> 00:13:41.987
Yeah those fries look like ass.

00:13:41.987 --> 00:13:46.425
And the next exclusive side
that we have is apple slices.

00:13:48.060 --> 00:13:50.663
Cut 'em up, put 'em in a plastic bag.

00:13:50.663 --> 00:13:53.632
'Bout to get saucy. That's
right, ladies and gentlemen.

00:13:56.836 --> 00:13:59.104
Sauce talk.

00:13:59.104 --> 00:14:00.172
Thank you.

00:14:01.273 --> 00:14:02.241
Spicy Buffalo.

00:14:03.776 --> 00:14:04.810
Not that good.

00:14:04.810 --> 00:14:06.779
We got a tangy barbecue.

00:14:07.713 --> 00:14:08.547
Ooh.

00:14:10.015 --> 00:14:10.916
Much better.

00:14:10.916 --> 00:14:12.852
Mm. Honey mustard.

00:14:15.354 --> 00:14:16.555
Tastes like salad dressing.

00:14:16.555 --> 00:14:17.656
Sweet and sour.

00:14:19.458 --> 00:14:20.759
I would tie it with the tangy barbecue

00:14:20.759 --> 00:14:23.128
because it's so different,
so we'll keep these guys

00:14:23.128 --> 00:14:24.230
same tier.

00:14:24.230 --> 00:14:27.299
Ranch, I don't know.
America, we love our ranch.

00:14:27.299 --> 00:14:28.267
Ranch is just OK.

00:14:28.267 --> 00:14:30.636
That's right, I said it. Ranch is just OK.

00:14:30.636 --> 00:14:34.240
Oh, and all ranch tastes the same. Yeah.

00:14:34.240 --> 00:14:35.841
And finally, honey.

00:14:38.010 --> 00:14:39.311
How do you like that?

00:14:39.311 --> 00:14:40.746
Honey's the best one.

00:14:40.746 --> 00:14:43.048
And all that money, all that energy,

00:14:43.048 --> 00:14:45.551
all that time creating all these recipes,

00:14:45.551 --> 00:14:48.821
trying to sway the American mind,

00:14:48.821 --> 00:14:52.658
and you got beat by a bunch of bees.

00:14:52.658 --> 00:14:54.793
Power to the bees!

00:14:54.793 --> 00:14:56.996
We have one exclusive spice mix

00:14:56.996 --> 00:14:59.164
as well as one exclusive
sauce here in India.

00:14:59.164 --> 00:15:01.267
We have chili sauce, which
is pretty straightforward.

00:15:01.267 --> 00:15:02.368
It's chili sauce.

00:15:02.368 --> 00:15:04.403
But let me tell you about

00:15:04.403 --> 00:15:07.573
peri-peri spice mix.

00:15:07.573 --> 00:15:11.744
So, McDonald's launched
this in 2013 here in India,

00:15:11.744 --> 00:15:14.446
and it was so popular, there were riots

00:15:14.446 --> 00:15:15.848
when they said they were
going to discontinue it.

00:15:15.848 --> 00:15:19.551
And so now, it's a permanent
addition to the menu.

00:15:19.551 --> 00:15:21.787
First, you get this shake bag,

00:15:21.787 --> 00:15:23.822
then you grab your fries,

00:15:23.822 --> 00:15:26.025
and then you just pour that in there.

00:15:26.025 --> 00:15:26.892
Ah.

00:15:33.732 --> 00:15:35.901
Boom! Oh, boy.

00:15:35.901 --> 00:15:38.003
Can we cut to a before of the fries?

00:15:38.003 --> 00:15:41.607
You saw how they were. Now look at these.

00:15:41.607 --> 00:15:44.109
You can see the little flecks of spice

00:15:44.109 --> 00:15:46.145
just adorning each fry.

00:15:53.485 --> 00:15:54.853
Hello, it's Crystelle.

00:15:54.853 --> 00:15:57.856
And I know Nikhil has
peri-peri McDonald's chips,

00:15:57.856 --> 00:16:00.492
but in the UK, it is all about Nando's.

00:16:00.492 --> 00:16:01.794
Cheeky Nando's.

00:16:01.794 --> 00:16:03.495
Let's talk about peri-peri.

00:16:03.495 --> 00:16:06.165
Peri means pepper. And
it's a blend of spices,

00:16:06.165 --> 00:16:09.468
so it's got things like paprika,
ground bird's eye chili,

00:16:09.468 --> 00:16:11.904
a bit of oregano, a pinch
of ginger and cardamom,

00:16:11.904 --> 00:16:13.572
but it's a Portuguese spice blend.

00:16:13.572 --> 00:16:15.641
It's funny because
obviously Nikhil mentioned

00:16:15.641 --> 00:16:18.077
that the peri-peri fries
just blew off in India,

00:16:18.077 --> 00:16:20.346
and it makes sense, because I'm from Goa,

00:16:20.346 --> 00:16:21.847
which is in the south of India.

00:16:21.847 --> 00:16:24.116
Goa was colonized by the Portuguese.

00:16:24.116 --> 00:16:25.985
And so I really think that Indians

00:16:25.985 --> 00:16:27.920
are accustomed to that
Portuguese taste palate,

00:16:27.920 --> 00:16:31.757
which is why peri-peri fries
are doing so well in India.

00:16:31.757 --> 00:16:33.025
But enough of the talking.

00:16:33.025 --> 00:16:35.561
I want to dig into these
fries, because they look great.

00:16:35.561 --> 00:16:37.596
Mm. Oh, this is so good.

00:16:37.596 --> 00:16:39.098
Harry, get involved.

00:16:39.098 --> 00:16:40.132
You're not eating chips
without me, are you?

00:16:40.132 --> 00:16:42.101
Oh, sorry, I've already had a head start.

00:16:42.101 --> 00:16:43.402
Harry: Cheers.
Crystelle: Cheers.

00:16:44.403 --> 00:16:48.307
God damn, if that isn't like crack.

00:16:48.307 --> 00:16:49.274
For the early risers,

00:16:49.274 --> 00:16:51.577
there's plenty of
exclusive breakfast items

00:16:51.577 --> 00:16:52.911
at the US McDonald's.

00:16:52.911 --> 00:16:54.980
Sausage biscuit with egg.

00:16:54.980 --> 00:16:56.482
Next one,

00:16:56.482 --> 00:16:57.683
sausage biscuit.

00:16:57.683 --> 00:17:00.319
I mean, they take the
egg out, so it's just ...

00:17:00.319 --> 00:17:03.722
This, of course, is
bacon, egg, and cheese.

00:17:03.722 --> 00:17:04.723
Ladies and gentlemen,

00:17:04.723 --> 00:17:06.291
we've reached the point of the breakfast

00:17:06.291 --> 00:17:07.893
where we get into the McGriddles.

00:17:07.893 --> 00:17:08.961
I love McGriddles.

00:17:08.961 --> 00:17:11.563
What's a McGriddle, you ask,
India? Fantastic question.

00:17:11.563 --> 00:17:14.333
McDonald's had this genius idea

00:17:14.333 --> 00:17:17.102
to replace the breakfast
sandwiches they already had

00:17:17.102 --> 00:17:18.737
with pancakes.

00:17:18.737 --> 00:17:22.808
And they also, like, inject
syrup into it somehow?

00:17:22.808 --> 00:17:26.779
But it is a breakfast sandwich
with pancakes for buns,

00:17:26.779 --> 00:17:31.150
and it's the best idea anyone's
ever had, anywhere, ever.

00:17:31.150 --> 00:17:34.686
[Joe laughing]

00:17:34.686 --> 00:17:36.288
Look at this! Look at this, look at this.

00:17:36.288 --> 00:17:38.223
They've even got a little M on there.

00:17:38.223 --> 00:17:39.391
This mini pancake.

00:17:39.391 --> 00:17:41.393
I know I'm wearing the
gloves, but this one's mine.

00:17:42.861 --> 00:17:43.729
Mm.

00:17:43.729 --> 00:17:47.699
We have a veg McMuffin
and a sausage McMuffin.

00:17:49.201 --> 00:17:50.035
Mm.

00:17:50.035 --> 00:17:52.671
The sausage here in India
is not made out of pork,

00:17:52.671 --> 00:17:54.006
like it is in the US.

00:17:54.006 --> 00:17:56.508
Instead, it's made out of simple chicken.

00:17:56.508 --> 00:18:00.012
Speaking of sausage, you
can get a breakfast burrito.

00:18:01.513 --> 00:18:04.283
Bro, I could put five of
these away, easy. Easy.

00:18:04.283 --> 00:18:06.351
If you're, like, a total drag

00:18:06.351 --> 00:18:09.054
and you want oatmeal in
the morning, we have it.

00:18:09.054 --> 00:18:11.423
It's about as inspiring
as you would think.

00:18:11.423 --> 00:18:12.991
Hotcakes and sausage.

00:18:12.991 --> 00:18:15.227
Of course, it comes with hot syrup.

00:18:15.227 --> 00:18:16.261
This here,

00:18:17.496 --> 00:18:19.598
the big breakfast with hotcakes.

00:18:19.598 --> 00:18:20.632
And it's big.

00:18:20.632 --> 00:18:23.469
A lot of eggs, kind of
wimpy-looking bacon,

00:18:23.469 --> 00:18:26.271
got yourself two English muffins here.

00:18:26.271 --> 00:18:29.274
And, of course, comes with a hash brown.

00:18:29.274 --> 00:18:31.243
Potatoes. Who doesn't love 'em?

00:18:31.243 --> 00:18:33.378
McDonald's hash brown, undefeated.

00:18:33.378 --> 00:18:34.346
These things are so good.

00:18:34.346 --> 00:18:36.148
India exclusive desserts.

00:18:36.148 --> 00:18:39.151
We have a Black Forest McFlurry,

00:18:39.151 --> 00:18:41.019
a vanilla chocolate muffin,

00:18:41.019 --> 00:18:43.455
and a chocolate chip muffin.

00:18:43.455 --> 00:18:46.458
It's kind of like a
McFlurry soup right now.

00:18:48.260 --> 00:18:51.797
This would be really good when
it was actually a McFlurry.

00:18:51.797 --> 00:18:54.199
Desserts! USA, we got 'em.

00:18:54.199 --> 00:18:55.834
So, starting down here, very simple,

00:18:55.834 --> 00:18:57.669
chocolate chip cookies.

00:18:57.669 --> 00:18:59.538
This next thing, apple fritter, right?

00:19:00.739 --> 00:19:01.840
Mm.

00:19:01.840 --> 00:19:05.043
This right here is called a
glazed pull-apart doughnut.

00:19:05.043 --> 00:19:06.178
Blueberry muffin.

00:19:06.178 --> 00:19:07.412
If you've had one, you've had them all.

00:19:07.412 --> 00:19:08.680
This is a what type of pie?

00:19:08.747 --> 00:19:10.315
Anders: A guava and cream pie. 

00:19:10.315 --> 00:19:11.717
Let's see what's inside.

00:19:11.717 --> 00:19:14.953
OK. I'm suddenly more interested. Yeah!

00:19:14.953 --> 00:19:16.955
Guava and cream.

00:19:16.955 --> 00:19:19.558
How about we'll call it
the cream and guava pie?

00:19:19.558 --> 00:19:20.692
Nah, this sucks.

00:19:20.692 --> 00:19:22.161
[Anders laughing]

00:19:22.995 --> 00:19:23.996
I don't f--- with it.

00:19:23.996 --> 00:19:26.698
Standard menu item, the
McDonald's apple pie.

00:19:26.698 --> 00:19:27.533
Everyone knows about this.

00:19:27.533 --> 00:19:29.868
I don't want a pizza version of this.

00:19:29.868 --> 00:19:32.905
Eh! And last but not least, cinnamon roll.

00:19:32.905 --> 00:19:34.173
Too sticky. I don't feel like eating it.

00:19:38.243 --> 00:19:39.878
Update: It's not sticky.

00:19:39.878 --> 00:19:42.281
It's actually [knocks on cinnamon roll].

00:19:42.281 --> 00:19:44.583
Exclusive drinks, starting with,

00:19:44.583 --> 00:19:46.218
we have something called

00:19:46.218 --> 00:19:49.721
B Natural's mixed fruit juice.

00:19:49.721 --> 00:19:50.889
Next up, we have something

00:19:50.889 --> 00:19:54.927
that they call raw mango fruit splash.

00:19:54.927 --> 00:19:56.094
Oh!

00:19:56.094 --> 00:19:57.596
It's a bit too sweet.

00:19:57.596 --> 00:19:59.698
Berry lemonade splash.

00:19:59.698 --> 00:20:03.368
All of these come in these very unique

00:20:03.368 --> 00:20:05.737
reusable bottles, apparently.

00:20:05.737 --> 00:20:09.908
Next up, strawberry chiller,
green apple chiller,

00:20:09.908 --> 00:20:12.878
and lemon chiller.

00:20:14.046 --> 00:20:16.448
It's just flavored water.
That's exactly what it is.

00:20:16.448 --> 00:20:18.984
It's flavored water,
and I kind of like it.

00:20:18.984 --> 00:20:21.520
This is a mixed berry smoothie.

00:20:23.555 --> 00:20:25.457
It's still quite sweet, but quite good.

00:20:25.457 --> 00:20:28.060
Next up, American mud pie shake.

00:20:29.528 --> 00:20:32.231
Mm. That's pretty yum.

00:20:32.231 --> 00:20:33.699
Drink roulette.

00:20:33.699 --> 00:20:35.968
Ooh, and the ice melted. Fantastic.

00:20:35.968 --> 00:20:38.670
Dr. Pepper. Let's go!

00:20:38.670 --> 00:20:41.440
Coke, nonexclusive. Let's go.

00:20:41.440 --> 00:20:42.941
Sweet tea, too sweet.

00:20:44.409 --> 00:20:46.645
Ugh, yeah. Unsweetened
tea, not sweet enough.

00:20:46.645 --> 00:20:47.713
You guys combine.

00:20:47.713 --> 00:20:50.182
For the kids watching,
why are you watching?

00:20:50.182 --> 00:20:52.017
Where are your parents or supervisors?

00:20:52.017 --> 00:20:54.720
You can get yourself apple juice, milk.

00:20:54.720 --> 00:20:56.188
Come on, you're drinking milk?

00:20:56.188 --> 00:20:57.456
The thought of drinking straight milk,

00:20:57.456 --> 00:20:58.657
like, hurts my stomach.

00:20:58.657 --> 00:21:00.158
There's also chocolate milk on the menu.

00:21:00.158 --> 00:21:01.126
Once upon a time,

00:21:01.126 --> 00:21:04.096
this was an iced French vanilla latte.

00:21:04.096 --> 00:21:07.165
Now it's more of a room-temperature
French vanilla latte.

00:21:09.001 --> 00:21:11.136
That's just OK. It's, like, really sweet.

00:21:11.136 --> 00:21:12.738
Strawberry banana smoothie.

00:21:13.805 --> 00:21:15.274
Yeah, I always loved getting these.

00:21:15.274 --> 00:21:16.375
These are good.

00:21:16.375 --> 00:21:18.477
So I'm going to assume
they're not good for me.

00:21:18.477 --> 00:21:19.911
Exclusive hot drinks.

00:21:19.911 --> 00:21:22.481
First off, we have strawberry green tea.

00:21:22.481 --> 00:21:25.217
Next up, English breakfast tea

00:21:25.217 --> 00:21:27.519
and Moroccan tea.

00:21:27.519 --> 00:21:29.955
Next up, a flat white coffee.

00:21:29.955 --> 00:21:33.392
India, a land where we run on chai,

00:21:33.392 --> 00:21:36.295
and McDonald's does
not have a chai option.

00:21:36.295 --> 00:21:37.996
Caramel macchiato,

00:21:37.996 --> 00:21:39.931
cappuccino,

00:21:39.931 --> 00:21:41.133
caramel latte,

00:21:41.133 --> 00:21:42.200
a vanilla cappuccino.

00:21:42.200 --> 00:21:44.236
The V does look like a U.

00:21:44.236 --> 00:21:47.439
McDonald's premium roast coffee.

00:21:49.374 --> 00:21:50.575
I'm going to hang on to this one.

00:21:52.911 --> 00:21:56.481
In India, a chicken Maharaja
Mac will cost you 231 rupees

00:21:56.481 --> 00:21:57.649
for just the sandwich.

00:21:57.649 --> 00:22:00.319
That's around $3.03.

00:22:00.319 --> 00:22:02.387
We do not have the chicken Maharaja Mac,

00:22:02.387 --> 00:22:04.056
but we do have the Big Mac,

00:22:04.056 --> 00:22:07.359
and a Big Mac in the US costs $4.89.

00:22:07.359 --> 00:22:10.362
That is a 61% price increase.

00:22:10.362 --> 00:22:12.431
Now, what if you turn this into a meal?

00:22:12.431 --> 00:22:15.534
A McSaver Maharaja Mac combo
comes with regular fries

00:22:15.534 --> 00:22:19.571
and a regular drink and
will cost you 356 rupees.

00:22:19.571 --> 00:22:22.941
That is $4.67, still less than the price

00:22:22.941 --> 00:22:24.943
of the American sandwich on its own.

00:22:24.943 --> 00:22:27.346
But does the combo meal
make a difference in the US?

00:22:27.346 --> 00:22:28.613
A medium Big Mac combo,

00:22:28.613 --> 00:22:31.583
so Big Mac, medium fries, medium drink,

00:22:31.583 --> 00:22:33.819
is $8.99.

00:22:33.819 --> 00:22:37.122
That's a 92% cost increase,

00:22:37.122 --> 00:22:39.758
even worse than if you just
bought the sandwich on its own.

00:22:39.758 --> 00:22:41.393
On the Indian McDonald's menu,

00:22:41.393 --> 00:22:42.794
you'll find a two-person meal,

00:22:42.794 --> 00:22:46.031
which contains a chicken
Maharaja Mac, a veg Maharaja Mac,

00:22:46.031 --> 00:22:50.001
large fries, two pizza
McPuffs, and a drink.

00:22:50.001 --> 00:22:54.639
All of this will cost
you 681 rupees, or $8.93.

00:22:54.639 --> 00:22:56.708
So, basically, you're
getting food for two people

00:22:56.708 --> 00:22:59.544
for the price of one
person's meal in the US.

00:22:59.544 --> 00:23:01.346
However, while it seems a lot cheaper

00:23:01.346 --> 00:23:03.215
than the food in the US,

00:23:03.215 --> 00:23:04.783
it's still very expensive

00:23:04.783 --> 00:23:07.152
and aspirational to people over here.

00:23:07.152 --> 00:23:09.221
Your minimum wage per hour

00:23:09.221 --> 00:23:11.556
is equal to our daily minimum wage.

00:23:11.556 --> 00:23:12.657
And so, yeah,

00:23:12.657 --> 00:23:14.826
a lot of people can't really
afford this kind of food.

00:23:14.826 --> 00:23:16.461
The English-speaking Indians that you see

00:23:16.461 --> 00:23:19.197
in a lot of YouTube videos on the internet

00:23:19.197 --> 00:23:20.632
aren't really a proper reflection

00:23:20.632 --> 00:23:22.667
of the majority of people
that live in this country,

00:23:22.667 --> 00:23:24.770
who still can't afford food like this.

00:23:24.770 --> 00:23:27.038
So, I'm checking my privilege,

00:23:27.038 --> 00:23:28.907
and we should all make sure we check ours.

00:23:28.907 --> 00:23:30.509
But let's play devil's advocate.

00:23:30.509 --> 00:23:32.811
McDonald's India has definitely included

00:23:32.811 --> 00:23:35.313
a lot more affordable
options on their menu.

00:23:35.313 --> 00:23:37.616
And so they are more approachable

00:23:37.616 --> 00:23:40.819
to the average urban Indian
than other fast-food chains.

00:23:44.289 --> 00:23:45.323
Let's compare some items

00:23:45.323 --> 00:23:48.693
to see who has the least
healthy McDonald's food.

00:23:48.693 --> 00:23:52.297
In the US, a McChicken
contains 400 calories,

00:23:52.297 --> 00:23:55.634
21 grams of fat, 39 grams of carbs.

00:23:55.634 --> 00:23:57.169
5 of those are sugar,

00:23:57.169 --> 00:23:59.538
and 560 milligrams of sodium.

00:23:59.538 --> 00:24:01.072
How about the Indian McChicken?

00:24:01.072 --> 00:24:03.975
One of these contains 398 calories,

00:24:03.975 --> 00:24:06.511
15 grams of total fat, 48 grams of carbs,

00:24:06.511 --> 00:24:08.647
5 grams of which are sugars,

00:24:08.647 --> 00:24:11.650
787 milligrams of sodium.

00:24:11.650 --> 00:24:15.287
So the Indian version has
slightly fewer calories,

00:24:15.287 --> 00:24:19.357
way lesser fats, but much
more carbs and sodium.

00:24:19.357 --> 00:24:20.659
What if we made that a combo meal?

00:24:20.659 --> 00:24:23.528
Well, a medium fry in the
US contains the following:

00:24:23.528 --> 00:24:26.431
320 calories, 15 grams of total fat,

00:24:26.431 --> 00:24:28.834
43 grams of carbs, no sugar,

00:24:28.834 --> 00:24:31.002
and 260 milligrams of sodium.

00:24:31.002 --> 00:24:34.706
While a medium fries in
India contains 340 calories,

00:24:34.706 --> 00:24:37.909
17 grams of total fat, 41 grams of carbs,

00:24:37.909 --> 00:24:39.411
0 grams of sugars,

00:24:39.411 --> 00:24:42.714
and 256 milligrams of sodium.

00:24:42.714 --> 00:24:45.283
And if we add the medium Coke,

00:24:45.283 --> 00:24:48.753
that is adding 210 calories, no fat,

00:24:48.753 --> 00:24:51.656
56 grams of carbs, 56 of those are sugar,

00:24:51.656 --> 00:24:53.925
and 55 milligrams of sodium.

00:24:53.925 --> 00:24:55.727
Ooh, a nice salty Coke.

00:24:55.727 --> 00:24:57.195
We'll do the same. Here in India,

00:24:57.195 --> 00:25:00.699
one medium Coke will
cost you 151 calories,

00:25:00.699 --> 00:25:03.368
0 grams of fat, 38 grams of carbs,

00:25:03.368 --> 00:25:05.837
38 grams of which are sugars,

00:25:05.837 --> 00:25:08.707
and there are 0 grams
of sodium, but my God,

00:25:08.707 --> 00:25:11.743
that is a lot of sugar packed in this cup.

00:25:11.743 --> 00:25:13.845
That leaves the Indian
meal at a grand total

00:25:13.845 --> 00:25:17.282
of 889 calories, 32 grams of fat,

00:25:17.282 --> 00:25:19.117
127 grams of carbs,

00:25:19.117 --> 00:25:20.952
out of which 43 grams are sugars,

00:25:20.952 --> 00:25:25.590
and 1,043 milligrams of sodium.

00:25:25.590 --> 00:25:26.491
Sheesh.

00:25:26.491 --> 00:25:29.327
Which means this whole bad boy altogether

00:25:29.327 --> 00:25:31.363
is 930 calories,

00:25:31.363 --> 00:25:32.898
36 grams of total fat,

00:25:32.898 --> 00:25:34.366
138 grams of carbs,

00:25:34.366 --> 00:25:36.568
61 of those grams are sugar,

00:25:36.568 --> 00:25:39.371
875 milligrams of sodium.

00:25:39.371 --> 00:25:42.173
Little bit lower sodium than India,

00:25:42.173 --> 00:25:46.478
but we got you guys beat in
calorie, fats, carbs, and sugar.

00:25:46.478 --> 00:25:50.615
Mm, mm, mm, mm! We win. We win.

00:25:50.615 --> 00:25:51.716
Ah!

00:25:51.716 --> 00:25:52.684
Unfortunately for India,

00:25:52.684 --> 00:25:54.419
the combo stats are a little misleading,

00:25:54.419 --> 00:25:56.488
and the difference maker is the Coke,

00:25:56.488 --> 00:25:59.324
because the American meal
has a larger portion.

00:25:59.324 --> 00:26:02.127
If you order the Coke
Zero in both countries,

00:26:02.127 --> 00:26:05.096
the Indian meal will actually
have a higher calorie count.

00:26:07.566 --> 00:26:09.601
McDonald's India does
not share a full list

00:26:09.601 --> 00:26:10.802
of their ingredients,

00:26:10.802 --> 00:26:13.738
but there are some things
we do know about their food.

00:26:13.738 --> 00:26:14.973
Like, did you know that McDonald's India

00:26:14.973 --> 00:26:17.142
actually changed Indian farming practices

00:26:17.142 --> 00:26:19.844
just so they could grow the
kind of potato that they wanted?

00:26:19.844 --> 00:26:22.180
When they first launched in India in 1996,

00:26:22.180 --> 00:26:23.615
McDonald's promised the government

00:26:23.615 --> 00:26:25.283
that they would use products grown

00:26:25.283 --> 00:26:27.218
and sourced right here in India.

00:26:27.218 --> 00:26:29.254
But people who had eaten McDonald's abroad

00:26:29.254 --> 00:26:32.290
realized that the fries
didn't taste quite the same.

00:26:32.290 --> 00:26:33.959
The reason for this is
that Indian potatoes

00:26:33.959 --> 00:26:35.327
were too small, round,

00:26:35.327 --> 00:26:37.896
had way too much moisture
and sugar content.

00:26:37.896 --> 00:26:41.066
And so the fries made out of
them were not long enough,

00:26:41.066 --> 00:26:43.401
they didn't get crispy
enough, and they didn't have

00:26:43.401 --> 00:26:46.371
that distinctive McDonald's oomph to them.

00:26:46.371 --> 00:26:48.873
So, McDonald's partnered
with McCain Foods,

00:26:48.873 --> 00:26:52.577
and they spent nine years
trying to perfect their potato.

00:26:52.577 --> 00:26:55.380
They imported saplings
which had the perfect shape

00:26:55.380 --> 00:26:57.148
and starch content that they needed.

00:26:57.148 --> 00:26:59.351
They also chose Gujarat
as their farming location

00:26:59.351 --> 00:27:00.819
for its climate, and they switched

00:27:00.819 --> 00:27:03.722
from a flood irrigation
to a sprinkler system

00:27:03.722 --> 00:27:06.358
to reduce moisture content and save water.

00:27:06.358 --> 00:27:09.494
The result: bigger and
more starchy potatoes

00:27:09.494 --> 00:27:11.463
that can be used to make
the McDonald's fries

00:27:11.463 --> 00:27:13.231
that you know and love.

00:27:13.231 --> 00:27:16.468
McDonald's in the US
mostly uses russet Burbank

00:27:16.468 --> 00:27:20.005
or Shepody, "shep-a-tee," potatoes.

00:27:20.005 --> 00:27:21.640
Potato me.

00:27:21.640 --> 00:27:26.177
So, these are big enough that
the distinctive long fry,

00:27:26.177 --> 00:27:28.847
yeah, look how long this is. Wow!

00:27:28.847 --> 00:27:31.916
Known to be low moisture
and low sugar content.

00:27:31.916 --> 00:27:34.285
This means they can
remain crispy when fried

00:27:34.285 --> 00:27:35.854
and don't caramelize too fast,

00:27:35.854 --> 00:27:38.490
so you can get a nice, even browning.

00:27:38.490 --> 00:27:40.725
McDonald's in the US actually discloses

00:27:40.725 --> 00:27:41.760
all of its ingredients,

00:27:41.760 --> 00:27:44.029
so we can figure out a
few other differences.

00:27:44.029 --> 00:27:45.296
In the US, for instance,

00:27:45.296 --> 00:27:47.599
our mayonnaise contains egg yolk,

00:27:47.599 --> 00:27:49.534
as does most American mayo.

00:27:49.534 --> 00:27:52.337
Thanks to the FAQ page on
the McDonald's India website,

00:27:52.337 --> 00:27:54.706
we found out that the
mayonnaise is eggless,

00:27:54.706 --> 00:27:56.074
along with all of the other sauces

00:27:56.074 --> 00:27:57.742
except for the tartar sauce.

00:27:57.742 --> 00:28:00.445
When people describe things
as vegetarian here in India,

00:28:00.445 --> 00:28:02.947
they typically mean it
doesn't contain egg.

00:28:02.947 --> 00:28:05.383
Did we quietly retire 
Ronald and the crew?

00:28:05.383 --> 00:28:06.818
If we did, thank God.

00:28:06.818 --> 00:28:08.920
It was very bizarre, the
whole Ronald McDonald thing.

00:28:08.920 --> 00:28:13.024
It's kind of nightmarish.
So, away he goes.

